<Site title="Editorial limits"><section class="wrap narrow page-head"><p class="kicker">READ WITH CONTEXT</p><h1>Sources & editorial limits.</h1><div class="prose"><p>This read-only interface preserves the original archive. Claims remain unreviewed and rights unknown unless a record explicitly describes more limited inspected material. A link, catalogue record or passing engineering check is not historical authentication.</p><p>Samuel Johnson’s books are excluded as factual authorities. Indirect reliance through other authors requires human source-of-source review. Akinwumi Ogundiran’s book is a reading lead, not permission to infer unread page claims.</p><p>Community accounts need consent, named attribution and regional context. Sacred or restricted knowledge is not automatically public because it can be found online. Oral tradition, religious belief, scholarly interpretation and scientific evidence must remain distinguishable.</p><p>The author dossiers retain edition and access limitations. No Yoruba audio, Ifá verse, historical claim or reference is fabricated for this interface. Medical and supernatural claims are not promoted to proven facts.</p><p>Community submissions, accounts, uploads and public hosting are outside this engineering preview. The local Python pilot is not a production service.</p></div><a href="/sources/">Explore the preserved source catalogue →</a></section></Site>
